# PORT-SUN-ROTATION: a directional light is aimed by its Rotation (forward -Z), as UE's ULightComponent::GetDirection;
# Translation no longer encodes a direction. Every scene/prefab is raised by the light chain (LGHT v1, SceneMigrator
# MigrateLightRotationV0ToV1). Details shows ONE direction widget on the sun: compass + horizon arc + Elevation/Azimuth.
# The Starter sun is entity 13376537502658031226 ("Sun").
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Тогда 1_migrated frame and shadows as on dev before the migration (the sun lights from the same place); Details on Sun shows the Sun Direction widget
# The widget's Elevation number, through the same rule (Rules::SunAngles -> AimDirectionalLight, one undo step).
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation 5
Тогда 2_low_sun long shadows, sunset sky; Details: one direction widget (compass + horizon arc, Elevation 5.0), no second direction control
# The rotate gizmo's write: the same TransformCommand, the azimuth turned by 90 deg.
Когда run Transform Rotate
Когда --subject selection set SunAzimuth 90
Тогда 3_gizmo shadows turned by 90 deg; the widget shows the new azimuth
Когда run Action Undo
Когда run Action Undo
Тогда 4_undo frame as 1_migrated
